  <!-- 3. DELTA -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>UNGA high-level week opened September 22 in New York with Iranian FM Araghchi and US Secretary of State Rubio both in attendance for separate bilateral programs. No scheduled direct or third-party-mediated session between US and Iranian officials has been confirmed; Oman stated it submitted a corridor-meeting arrangement request to the Iranian delegation that had not been acknowledged by the September 22 morning news cycle (Al Jazeera, Reuters). → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>The de facto fire pause on the Lebanese front entered its 13th day without a major cross-border incident as of September 22. UNIFIL reported no artillery exchanges between Israeli forces and IRGC-affiliated units since September 9. Both sides have maintained deniability postures through French and UN intermediary channels. IRGC resupply convoys were observed transiting the Bekaa valley on September 19–20 per satellite imagery cited by OSINT analysts, without triggering an Israeli counterstrike. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>Straits.live AIS tracking recorded the Strait of Hormuz as effectively closed to commercial traffic on September 21, with approximately 401 vessels holding in Persian Gulf anchorages pending safe-passage assurance. The IRGC-enforced restricted zone in the northern Hormuz approaches, activated September 7, remained in force as of September 22. Iran's Supreme National Security Council on September 20 issued a public three-condition linkage — US strike halt, full sanctions lifting, and written security guarantees — as explicit preconditions for any Hormuz transit normalization. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>
      <p>Israeli polls conducted after the September 15 party-list closure deadline showed Yashar (Eisenkot) leading in 4 of 5 published surveys with 24–25 seats against Likud's 21–23. A Channel 12 poll on September 20 recorded Yashar at 25 seats and Likud at 22, the widest margin of the campaign to date. The ultra-Orthodox draft controversy and Netanyahu's association with the ongoing Iran conflict have not produced a patriotic-rally consolidation effect among the electorate. → moved <span class="cite">F5</span></p>
      <p>US diplomatic engagement has focused on the UNGA margins, with the State Department confirming Rubio would hold bilateral meetings with Gulf partners on September 22–23. No new ceasefire proposal framework has been announced as of the September 22 morning news cycle. Qatar and Pakistan continued sub-ministerial message-relay operations between Washington and Tehran. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

